(7553491, 1209990, 123833, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rooum:</b></div><hr/><i> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by marnet:</b></div><hr/><i> I feel sorry for her </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Oh, don''t feel sorry for her Margaret, she''s an incredibly happy child - always laughing and smiling. She doesn''t like having her photo taken though so pretty much all my photos of her are when she''s daydreaming and thinking or scowling at the camera which I think gives a bit of a skewed view of her. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Is this your daughter?? That''s different, you would have many opportunities to take photos of her in different moods, I thought it was one photo of a child from one of your weddings. <br/> <br/>I will add that you are incredibly good at photos of the people. They are exceptional.</td>', 'Originally posted by rooum: Originally posted by marnet: I feel sorry for her   Oh, don''t feel sorry for her Margaret, she''s an incredibly happy child - always laughing and smiling. She doesn''t like having her photo taken though so pretty much all my photos of her are when she''s daydreaming and thinking or scowling at the camera which I think gives a bit of a skewed view of her.  Is this your daughter?? That''s different, you would have many opportunities to take photos of her in different moods, I thought it was one photo of a child from one of your weddings.  I will add that you are incredibly good at photos of the people. They are exceptional.', '2018-01-20 13:25:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(7553498, 1210174, 104230, '<td valign="top">I love the white glove.  It looks like someone reaching up from behind the steeping wheel, and I don''t know why but I feel a thread stretching from that to the man''s head.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2018-01-20 18:11:49.</i></td>', 'I love the white glove.  It looks like someone reaching up from behind the steeping wheel, and I don''t know why but I feel a thread stretching from that to the man''s head.', '2018-01-20 15:51:19.000000', '2018-01-20 18:11:49.000000', 0),
(7553501, 1210258, 100831, '<td valign="top">I admit, I did not give this photo the merit it deserved (score of 6).  It does indeed exude warmth and the back-light is magnificent.</td>', 'I admit, I did not give this photo the merit it deserved (score of 6).  It does indeed exude warmth and the back-light is magnificent.', '2018-01-20 16:37:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(7553509, 1209875, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An image that contributes to the challenge<br/> <br/>Your portrait fulfils the challenge brief in that it has been taken in natural light, there are however, a few things that I may suggest as potential improvements. There is a lot of distracting background that competes with the main subject as a result of the chosen aperture which has given you too much DOF. Most good portraits isolate the model from the background through use of (often) maximum aperture, sufficient distance between the subject and the background and by moving in closer to also reduce DOF. The composition is very central, use of thirds would greatly improve impact and also use of landscape orientation would enable you to make more use of the scene to add impact to the end result. I can see that you would want to include his kilt so a cropped composition just above the hem line and just above his head with landscape orientation with him to the left hrizontal third would have greatly improved the impact. Hope this helps a little Ellie, keep at it...</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An image that contributes to the challenge Your portrait fulfils the challenge brief in that it has been taken in natural light, there are however, a few things that I may suggest as potential improvements. There is a lot of distracting background that competes with the main subject as a result of the chosen aperture which has given you too much DOF. Most good portraits isolate the model from the background through use of (often) maximum aperture, sufficient distance between the subject and the background and by moving in closer to also reduce DOF. The composition is very central, use of thirds would greatly improve impact and also use of landscape orientation would enable you to make more use of the scene to add impact to the end result. I can see that you would want to include his kilt so a cropped composition just above the hem line and just above his head with landscape orientation with him to the left hrizontal third would have greatly improved the impact. Hope this helps a little Ellie, keep at it...', '2018-01-20 16:59:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(7553515, 1210069, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge<br/> <br/>I like your lovely natural light mono portrait Cole, it is very accomplished. However, I also have reservations about the right eye, it looks unnatural because there is by contrast too much light falling on her iris, it is too bleached which unfortunately is often associated with the look of visual impairment or blindness. It''s such a shame because the rest of the portrait works really well and although its such a seemingly minor fault it has a significant impact on the end result. The high score and placement serves to confirm what a strong image the rest of it is, well done.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that contributes well to the challenge I like your lovely natural light mono portrait Cole, it is very accomplished. However, I also have reservations about the right eye, it looks unnatural because there is by contrast too much light falling on her iris, it is too bleached which unfortunately is often associated with the look of visual impairment or blindness. It''s such a shame because the rest of the portrait works really well and although its such a seemingly minor fault it has a significant impact on the end result. The high score and placement serves to confirm what a strong image the rest of it is, well done.', '2018-01-20 17:10:39.000000', NULL, 0),
